    "description": "Ask the community for help",
    "emoji": ":pray:",
    "is_answerable": true
  },
  "labels": [],
  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "DC_kwDOKrJqmc4A7ncJ",
      "body": "On a few devices there is not enough disk space to upgrade rayhunter beyond the first installation, or the device will run out of disk space after a few recordings. Enforcing the sdcard seemed like a simpler thing than to try and support users who want to migrate their data from internal storage to the sdcard.\r\n\r\nexample of where this pans out on other devices: https://github.com/EFForg/rayhunter/issues/733",
      "author": {
        "login": "untitaker",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/837573?u=4b106f1ba83b3028677a861efe31c46d703e77ff&v=4",
        "url": "https://github.com/untitaker"
      },
      "created_at": "2026-01-28T11:58:10Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-28T11:58:56Z",
      "is_answer": true,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "DC_kwDOKrJqmc4A7oRH",
          "body": "Thanks for reaction.\n\nHmmm, storage looks fine for me - just 27% used (19.6M used / 53.5M available). What is the average size of a recording? Or what was the threshold to move the installation to a sd-card?",
